## 5. Negative control, measured against the tree that lacks the deliverable

A worktree at the base commit, with only the new test file copied into it — no repository file was
moved, renamed or deleted anywhere in this workstream:

    $ git worktree add -q /tmp/negctl 52f682c8435956c8210b3189cad23ebea973d2de
    $ cp tests/test_milestone_deliverables.py /tmp/negctl/tests/
    $ cd /tmp/negctl && TMPDIR=/tmp python3 -m unittest tests.test_milestone_deliverables
      exit status 1
      FAIL: test_every_obliged_document_deliverable_exists
        AssertionError: Lists differ: [('M17', 'docs/playstation/SECURITY_BOUNDARY.md')] != []
      ERROR: test_m17_names_the_analysis_deliverable_and_it_is_substantive
        FileNotFoundError: … /tmp/negctl/docs/playstation/SECURITY_BOUNDARY.md
      Ran 4 tests in 0.002s
      FAILED (failures=1, errors=1)

So the check is not vacuous: it reports the exact gap it was written for, on the tree where the gap
exists, and stays silent about the milestones that are legitimately still missing their artifacts
(M18's loader, M19's boot evidence, M2d's kernel/usb/, the M1 record template's peers) — those four
were not reported, which is the scope property case 4 of the test pins.

    $ cd /home/user/pc5-m17work && TMPDIR=/tmp python3 -m unittest tests.test_milestone_deliverables
      exit 0, Ran 4 tests … OK
    $ git worktree remove --force /tmp/negctl
    $ git worktree list | wc -l -> 1
    $ git status --porcelain -> roadmap.json modified; three untracked paths; nothing else

