## 8. Nothing was executed, loaded or written

    $ git diff --name-only 52f682c8435956c8210b3189cad23ebea973d2de HEAD -- tools boot kernel psm src firmware
      (no output)
    $ ls /dev/sd* /dev/nvme*  -> No such file or directory (no block device of any kind)
    $ mknod /tmp/testnode b 8 0 -> mknod: Operation not permitted
      -> nothing was written because nothing could be: no device node exists and none can be made
    $ ls -l PS5UPDATE.PUP -> 135 bytes        (the pointer, as ADR-022 requires)
    $ TMPDIR=/tmp python3 tools/firmware.py analyze --input PS5UPDATE.PUP
      size 135 bytes
      sha256 6e8f5a459551316397f1946cce4d540a56c0b790854c2c0d94c442ca86e73b42
      kind unidentified - No documented signature matched.
      entropy mean 4.924 over 1 MiB windows
      -> the LFS POINTER was analysed, as always;
      the 1,423,697,408-byte payload was not fetched, not from LFS and not from any other host
    No Sony system software, no key material, no decrypted artifact and no console firmware exists in
    or was added to this workspace. No genuine target system software was loaded or executed, at any
    point, in any form. No physical-hardware validation was performed. No emulator was launched for
    this workstream (and `unicorn` is absent here, which is why the 109 skips exist).

## 9. Manifest

`HASHES.txt` in this directory records the identity of every file this workstream adds or modifies,
plus the whole of this evidence directory, generated by `gen_manifest.py` (committed here, run from
the repository root) after the last write to any recorded file. Verified with the recipe its own
header states; the result is recorded in the PR's fresh-clone comment, out-of-band, because a
manifest cannot describe the head that contains it.
